---
import Solution from '../../layouts/Solution.astro';
import MinimizationFunnel from '../../components/MinimizationFunnel.astro';
import SolutionFit from '../../components/SolutionFit.astro';
import DocsHandoff from '../../components/DocsHandoff.astro';
import { solutionAreas } from '../../data/solutions';
import { products } from '../../data/products';
const area = solutionAreas.find((a) => a.key === 'check-a-fact')!;
const tutorials = area.products.map((key) => products.find((p) => p.key === key)!);
---
<Solution
  area={area}
  heading="Let a service check a fact without receiving the record."
  description="A pension service needs to know whether a person is alive. A licensing service needs to know whether an applicant is 18 or older. Each can ask the register that holds the answer and receive only that answer, while the record stays with the institution that keeps it."
>
  <section id="example" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="check-example-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading center">
        <p class="eyebrow">One example: a civil register</p>
        <h2 id="check-example-title">One registry can support several services without sharing every field.</h2>
        <p>A pension service checks whether a person is alive. A licensing service checks whether they are 18 or older. The registry owner defines the permitted questions and access rules; Evidence Gateway applies those rules to each request.</p>
      </div>
      <MinimizationFunnel />
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="check-control-title">
    <div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">What the register owner decides</p>
        <h2 id="check-control-title">The question, who may ask it, and how long the answer holds.</h2>
        <p>Every register family has facts other services ask for: whether a licence is active, whether a supplier is registered, whether a household is enrolled. The team that keeps the register decides how each one is answered.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="product-facts">
        <article><h3>The question and its answer</h3><p>Agree what each answer means and how it is derived from the record. A residence region can be returned without the street address, and adult status without a date of birth.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Who may ask, and for what purpose</h3><p>Authorize each service for the questions and purposes agreed with it. A request outside those rules is refused, and each request and its outcome are recorded.</p></article>
        <article><h3>How long an answer holds</h3><p>Set how long an answer is valid. The receiving service checks the answer’s dates and signature before it relies on the answer.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="check-ai-title">
    <div class="section-inner product-fit">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI-assisted services</p>
        <h2 id="check-ai-title">The same access rules apply to an AI-assisted service.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>A service that uses AI to guide a person or caseworker can call the same configured Registry Stack interface as other services. Registry Stack checks the service’s permission for each request and returns only the information its rules allow.</p>
        <p>The choice is the same as for any other service: copy the records, or ask the question. A housing benefit service could receive a copy of each applicant’s income records and let its application work them out. Or the registry owner defines one question, such as whether annual net income is below the benefit threshold, and the registry returns that answer. The registry may hold gross monthly income while the rule needs net annual income; the definition of the question carries that translation, and the AI-assisted service never holds the record.</p>
        <p>The service owner remains responsible for how the application uses that information, including decisions about eligibility, approvals, and the people it makes requests about.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <SolutionFit
    area={area}
    heading="Choose a signed answer or agreed fields."
    jobs={{
      'evidence-gateway': 'Choose a signed answer when the service needs a yes or no, a status, or a band it can verify, such as adult status or registration status. The answer carries a signature showing which register issued it.',
      'protected-registry-apis': 'Choose agreed fields when the service needs values to work with, such as a business’s legal name and legal form, or a farmer’s registered status and farm size.',
    }}
    extra={[
      { term: 'The register stays where it is', body: 'Both can read from a register you already run, and neither requires Base Registry Engine. If you choose both, your technical team configures the connection.' },
    ]}
  >
    <p>A signed answer tells a service a fact. Agreed fields give it data it will process. Start from what the receiving service has to decide, and give it the least that decision needs.</p>
  </SolutionFit>
  <section id="developers" class="section section-muted" aria-labelledby="check-developers-title">
    <div class="section-inner product-fit">
      <div class="section-heading compact">
        <p class="eyebrow">For developers and implementers</p>
        <h2 id="check-developers-title">Run both exercises with sample data.</h2>
        <p>Each tutorial runs locally against a synthetic source and includes its own setup.</p>
      </div>
      <dl>
        {tutorials.map((product) => (
          <>
            <dt>{product.name}</dt>
            <dd>{product.firstResult} <a href={product.tutorialHref}>{product.tutorialLabel}</a>.</dd>
          </>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>
  <DocsHandoff eyebrow="Work with us" heading="Get help when you need it." body="Get hands-on help through a paid implementation pilot, or ongoing support while your team defines the questions and connects the register." emphasis="pilot" />
</Solution>
